        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: ವಂಶ",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ವಂಶ — vaṃśa — \"a lineage; a dynasty\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ಆ ವಂಶದ ರಾಜರು ಮುನ್ನೂರು ವರ್ಷ ಆಳಿದರು. ā vaṃśada rājaru munnūru varṣa āḷidaru. The kings of that dynasty ruled for three hundred years."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ವಂಶವೃಕ್ಷ is a family tree."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ವಂಶ (vaṃśa) is borrowed from Sanskrit vaṃśa, \"a bamboo cane\", and from its joints, \"a line of descent, a race\" (Monier-Williams)."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "One more word for telling what happened."
