          "title": "You'll want to know: ಅರಸ",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ಅರಸ — arasa — \"a monarch; a king\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ಆ ಅರಸ ಪ್ರಜೆಗಳಿಗಾಗಿ ಕೆರೆಗಳನ್ನು ಕಟ್ಟಿಸಿದನು. ā arasa prajegaḷigāgi keregaḷannu kaṭṭisidanu. That king had lakes built for his people."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Plural: ಅರಸರು, arasaru."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "An older Kannada form beside ರಾಜ; ಅರಮನೆ, a palace, is the king's house."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ಅರಸ (arasa) goes back to Sanskrit rājan, \"a chieftain, a king\" (CDIAL 10679): DEDR 201 lists Kannada arasa, arasu, \"a king, a lord\", and ara-mane, \"a palace\", and derives them from the Sanskrit word. It is an old reshaped loan, beside the learned ರಾಜ."
            }
          ]
        },
